# Official spec-kit install-time copy exclusion (gitignore syntax): everything
# listed here is development-only material that `specify extension add` must
# NEVER copy into a consuming repository's `.specify/extensions/jira/`.
# (This file itself is always excluded automatically.)
tests/
specs/
.specify/
.github/
.claude/
.tokensave/
.editorconfig
.gitignore
.shellcheckrc
PSScriptAnalyzerSettings.psd1
coverage.xml
# The coverage runner's output directory. It is gitignored, so it exists only on
# a machine that has measured coverage — but `specify extension add --dev` copies
# the working tree, not the git index, and this directory holds a NAMED PIPE
# (the xtrace fifo). Python's copytree refuses to copy one, so the install fails
# outright on any developer machine where the gate has been run.
coverage/
